                        


Item #:  SCP-5156

Object Class:  Keter

Special Containment Procedures:  Is to be locked in a glass container, and given an electric shock when found moving. Even the smallest movement must be seen and reported.

Description:  SCP-5156 has the look of an old, 19th-century wooden doll. Straw hair, with an early form of a tuxedo. Eyeless, with multiple knife wounds in and around the sockets. We believe that the man who tried to destroy SCP-5156 is now dead. No trace of him was found. Class-D personnel were subjected to testing the subject. Extremely difficult to contain, it can manipulate different materials within a range of 5 meters. Many different materials were tested, with the only partially successful trial material being glass. Dr.█████████ discovered that it had high amounts of energy can neutralize it for a short period of time. Further research from Class-D personnel concluded that  it's victims down to the molecular level. Communication with the anomaly is a work in progress, but it is able to answer yes and no questions by crumpling the paper with said answer. The only thing that it refuses to speak about is its origins and creation.

If experiencing nausea or drowsiness, notify an on-site staff, who will see you out and replace you for the day. If this continues, you may be seen as unfit to work in the sector. There will be 8 people in the observation room, two (2) on each side. There will be a lever to pull on each side that will send a 12v electric shock through the room, which will subdue the subject long enough for soldiers to pose at the ready. Similar to SCP-137, human eyes must be watching it at all times. Only small movements can be made when being watched. After seen moving, if human eyes leave it even for half a second, the anomaly can get close enough to the steel doors to breach. If breached, A glass shield will slide down in front of all doors, including doors to dangerous SCPs. If spotted, DO NOT ENGAGE. wait for other soldiers to come to your location. Stay at least 20ft away.  when backup comes, one man must get in range of a taser shot. This will subdue it for 2-3 minutes. Run as fast as you can back to the containment cell with the subject, and replace the glass case.

Further research is being conducted on this subject







                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    
                        
                            
